  DEFENDING ARMY

  Samantha led her armies into the fray.  No generals were present to lead 
the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  A bad omen appeared, which of course dealt a severe blow to Samantha's 
hopes.  Samantha's mount was shot and killed from under Samantha.  As the 
struggle developed, the tactical wit of the acting commander and Samantha 
appeared evenly matched.

  Across the whole front, the 115th Fleet Marines were arrayed against the 
Veteran 270th Bowmen.  The 115th Fleet Marines fought with the 270th Bowmen 
and were easily beaten by the enemy.
  The forces of the acting commander broke through and were victorious.  The 
270th Bowmen demolished the 115th Fleet Marines.
  The defenders defeated Samantha's forces and drove them out of the 
Buccaneer Sea.  Her forces completely destroyed, Samantha fled frightened 
and alone to the Amazonian Sea.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Kahn (#6)ian empire marched 
on the Forest province of Bronzeleaf, a land garrisoned by the forces of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Kahn was in command of the attacking 
armies.  The defenders were led by the provincial garrison commander.  The 
armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

