  Standing tall with his warriors was Kahn.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  An unfavorable omen appeared, which of course dealt a severe blow to Kahn
's hopes.  It seems that Kahn's mount was shot down while Kahn was giving a 
speech.  As the battle intensified, the tactical abilities of the acting 
commander and Kahn appeared evenly matched and neither general could gain a 
tactical advantage.

  Out on the right outside wing, the 218th Legion were aided in the battle 
by a band of medicine men sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which aroused 
them to a fanatical zeal.  They were arrayed against the 121st Garrison.  
The 220th Light Cavalry outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with full 
strength.  On this battleground, the 218th Legion audaciously charged their 
enemy, but became disordered and were thrown back by a well-timed, sustained 
countercharge.  Even so, the 218th Legion battled with the 121st Garrison 
and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 188th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
153rd Garrison.  In this area, the men of the 153rd Garrison encountered 
unpredictable footing and experienced confusion.  The 188th Bowmen fought 
with the 153rd Garrison and the fighting here proved inconclusive.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Uga-Buga Makumb, a 
final savage thrust defeated their enemy and won the day for Kahn.  The 
218th Legion scattered the 121st Garrison in all directions.  The 188th 
Bowmen chased after the enemy and annihilated the 153rd Garrison.
  Kahn's host concluded the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of Bronzeleaf.  The acting commander withdrew to the Callisto Sea, defeated 
but not broken.
  In late summer, Uga-Buga Makumb directed the 53rd Skeletal Phalanx, the 
267th Skeletal Chariots, the 70th Skeletal Chariots, the 155th Skeletal 
Chariots and the 83rd Skeletal Camel Corps to remain in Chaco with 
Constantine.
  The Daedalus Sea was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in 
the Daedalus Sea.
  With the coming of the fall season Uga-Buga Makumb flew over to Balmwood.  
To the west there is a Plain province known as Cantia (#403), a land of 
Humans where Prometeo reigns.  Their Human fighters array themselves in the 
style of Axemen and Light Cavalry.  Viewing the northwestern horizon, a man 
can see a Mountain province called St Helens (#402).  It is said that Hokuto 
reigns there.  It is known to be populated by Humans.  Their Human warriors 
traditionally array themselves in the style of Legion and Chariots.

  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded 
Balmwood, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Circe (#8) and made up of 
extensive Forests.  Uga-Buga Makumb's armies took possession of Balmwood 
practically uncontested.  Balmwood was found to have a tax base of 4 gold.

  Kahn (#6)'s forces initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Peachwood, 
a Forest province owing allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  
Hawkins (#56)'s forces experienced little resistance in Peachwood and 
Hawkins there established our reign.  Hawkins leads approximately 3 Bowmen.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb rode his flying 
armies into Silvermist.


  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
entered Silvermist, hoping to subjugate that province owned by Circe (#8) 
and made up of extensive Mountains.  Uga-Buga Makumb's forces encountered 
little opposition in Silvermist and Uga-Buga Makumb there established our 
rule.  Silvermist was discovered to have an income of 6 gold.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Attla (#54) arose one day with a desire to see St Helens, and so left from 
Silvermist to travel to that province.
  York (#67) heard that an old friend was pearl-diving in the Valiant Sea 
and left Ravenwood to see his old acquaintance.
  The 30th Eagles has wandered into Chaco from Katanga.
  The 213th Chariots lost hope of finding adventure in Berga, and so they 
mustered their strength and moved on to Chirfa.

  Starhaven was raided by the Gargoyle, who stormed from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 4 gold worth of property.  The Icaria Sea was raided 
by the Giant Wolverine, who came from out of the dark wilderness and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.  Sherwood was plundered by 
the Centaur, who came from out of the dark and pillaged or destroyed 3 gold 
worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 230 gold in revenue.  53 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 87th Garrison, the 88th Garrison, the 91st Dragons, the 150th 
Garrison and the 151st Garrison trained well and improved in quality.  143 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was left with 115 
gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I cast a Kill Enemy spell and Gladstone was magically killed by 
a dark Necromantic spell!  Thus did Gladstone die, a brave end by any 
standard.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I could not cast Kill Enemy on 
Charious because Charious was in another province.  So, I practiced my 
Tactics diligently for months, but could make no progress.
  With the coming of the late summer season Gladstone was resurrected by the 
spell cast by me.
  With the advent of the fall season, I could not cast Resurrection on 
Charious because Charious was still alive.  Instead, I practiced my Tactics 
well but could not improve my skill in Tactics.
  Gladstone cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed 
for me.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I moved into Quantara Roo 
(#1403) with my army.  East of here is Rejaf (#1503), a Desert province 
ruled by Kahn, where Elves dwell.  Their Elven fighters prefer to fight in 
the style of Camel Corps.  I found a feature in Quantara Roo: a Sacred Rock 
(#52) inhabited by the Sphinx.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  
Legend says that the Sphinx is a powerful winged monster with the body of a 
lion and the head of a man.  The Sphinx is very intelligent and loves to 
riddle.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Quantara Roo, a 
Plain area ruled by Kahn (#6).  Quantara Roo was conquered and occupied by 
Guerin's host.  Quantara Roo was discovered to have an income of 4 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Plague spell.  Cretacia was hit by a plague.  The 
Plague affected no armies in Cretacia.
  During early summer, I failed in my attempt to cast a Skeletal Army spell. 
My experience raised my prowess in Necromancy.
  All characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  With the coming of the late summer season I rode my flying armies over to 
Starhaven.  To the north icy wastes stretch to meet the far horizon.  The 
Platinum Wand senses the Crystal of Seeing in Starhaven.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Starhaven, a Forest province owing allegiance to Hokuto 
(#4).  I commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by 
Lexington (#48).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown 
here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Starhaven (0701):

