  The attackers had the 319th Eagles, the 321st Eagles and the 322nd Eagles 
in reserve.  I stood ready at the head of my thousands.  Lexington marched 
with his loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.
  I strode forward and challenged Lexington to personal combat.  Lexington 
accepted the challenge to honorable combat.  I incanted my strange words of 
magic and cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Lexington quake and shiver with 
spiritual convulsions.
  Lexington advanced to bow range.  Waving my hands, I orchestrated 
otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in 
the shape of a cross formed around me.
  Lexington charged into melee range.  Seeking to take advantage of a weak 
point in Teleko's protection, Lexington deftly swang at me but his sword 
whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Raising my hands high in the air, I 
cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with my hands. 
Lexington then thrust at me and would have hit me if I hadn't sidestepped 
just then.  I seized his neck with unseen hands and shook it and scored on 
Lexington, doing 3 points of damage.
  Lexington thrust at me but his sword whiffed harmlessly through the air.  
I clenched my fist tightly, squeezing the innards of Lexington and inflicted 3
damage points.  Lexington swang at his enemy and missed.  I brought my hands 
together and pulled them apart in a tearing motion, provoking a 
blood-curdling squeal from Lexington and damaged him, scoring 3 damage 
points.
  Lexington contemptuously thrust at me but his sword whiffed harmlessly 
through the air.  I brought my hands together and yanked them apart in a 
ripping gesture, provoking a squeal of pain from Lexington and inflicted 3 
damage points on him.  Lexington energetically swang at me and missed by a 
mile.  I curled my phantasmal hand around Lexington's liver and squeezed it 
viciously and scorched Lexington with 3 damage points.  Lexington fell, 
mortally injured.  Thus did Lexington finally die, a brave end by any 
standard.
  The forces commanded by Lexington were disheartened by his death, but 
still they moved forward with some hope of victory.  As luck would have it, 
Teleko's formations were well hidden by a sudden mist, giving them a small 
edge.  Also, tactical superiority was clearly assured by Teleko's powerful 
tactical genius.
  Hokuto (#4)'s soldiers were prepared to struggle like tigers for their 
homeland.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 323rd Trolls faced the 191st Legion.  
The 326th Dragons soared over the 191st Legion and attacked them.  The 323rd 
Trolls battled with the 191st Legion and cut them down like weeds.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Hokuto, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the battle for me.  
The 323rd Trolls destroyed the 191st Legion.
  Teleko's campaign effected the conquest of Starhaven.  Its forces 
completely dispersed, the acting commander escaped frightened and alone to 
Kilkenny.
  With the coming of the fall season I rode my flying armies over to 
Cretacia.  Viewing the western horizon, one can see a Forest province called 
Cherrywood (#501).  It is said that Hokuto reigns there.  It is known to be 
populated by Humans.  Their Human fighters fight as Bowmen and Light Cavalry.
To the north icy wastes stretch to join the horizon.  I was informed by some 
sheepherders of a feature in Cretacia previously unknown to us, a Volcanic 
Tunnel (#101) inhabited by the Green Dragon.  Legend says the Cloak of 
Stealth is hidden here.  The Green Dragon is a powerful dragon capable of 
breathing a poisonous cloud of gas.  The Platinum Wand senses the Cloak of 
Stealth in Cretacia.
  While talking to some friendly locals, I heard a rumor about a Cavern in 
Bir Nzaran (#1203), inhabited by the Ice Devil.  Some say that the Ice Devil 
actually owns the Huge Hoard of Gold.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Mountain province of Cretacia, 
