  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 77th Fleet Marines, the 97th Garrison and the 298th 
Garrison in reserve.  Tao-Li marched with his loyal troops, jaws set in grim 
determination.  Kurtinaitis led his armies boldly into the fray.
  Tao-Li's luck was terrible!  A thundercloud formed overhead and his 
vanguard was drenched by a dark thundershower.  This terrible omen 
completely disheartened his forces.  But his wise tactical maneuvers gave 
his side an undeniable superiority.

  Across the whole front, the Veteran 78th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
162nd Bowmen, who screamed their hideous war cries, goaded into a  fanatical 
frenzy by their diabolical King with false promises of plunder and slaves 
for all.  The 297th Axemen and the 296th Fleet Marines flanked the 
undermanned enemy lines and attacked with full strength.  Here, the 162nd 
Bowmen immediately turned to flight when they met their enemy.  But it soon 
became apparent that the retreat was a trick to lure their enemy onto more 
favorable ground.  The 78th Bowmen fought with the 162nd Bowmen and could 
not hold their ground against their determined foe.
  Kurtinaitis's armies vanquished the army opposing them with a final 
charge.  The 162nd Bowmen annihilated the 296th Fleet Marines.
  Tao-Li's armies were beaten and pushed out of the Plesiosaurus Sea.  The 
97th Garrison had no path of retreat and disbanded into mercenaries.  The 
298th Garrison could not retreat and were paroled into the population.  
Tao-Li retreated to Oceanus Cyclopia.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Tao-Li could not 
hire Kurtinaitis because Kurtinaitis rules his own province.  Instead, 
Tao-Li practiced his Psychic Magic well, and even consulted an astrologer, 
but could not improve his skill in Psychic Magic.
  In late summer, Tao-Li attempted an illegal move.  He was already in 
Oceanus Cyclopia and could make no sense of the order to move to Oceanus 
Cyclopia.  Instead, Tao-Li worked on his Meleeing but was thwarted in his 
efforts.
  In fall, Tao-Li attempted an illegal move.  He could not move to Mercia 
because armies can't move overland and use transport in the same turn.  So, 
Tao-Li tried to improve his Tactics, but the task was beyond his natural 
ability.
  With the coming of the early winter season Tao-Li could find no soldiers 
in Oceanus Cyclopia for the requested Whales troops.  Instead, Tao-Li tried 
to practice his Tactics, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Tao-Li


