  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 198th Trolls, the 333rd Bowmen, the 102nd Eagles and 
the 123rd Eagles in reserve.  I stood ready at the head of my thousands.  No 
generals were present to lead the forces of the provincial Dragon chieftain.
  The opposing armies raced for the high ground, and I obtained an advantage 
by getting there first.  Also, my clever tactical planning gave my side a 
clear advantage.

  Across the entire front, the Crack 334th Bowmen faced the 127th Dragons.  
The 206th Dragons swooped down on the 127th Dragons and attacked them.  The 
333rd Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged in with full strength.  The 
127th Dragons soared over the 334th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 
127th Dragons were decimated by the arrows loosed by those pesky Bowmen.  
The 334th Bowmen battled with the 127th Dragons and trampled them down as if 
they were midgets.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Odysseus as they broke 
through the lines at a critical moment.  The 334th Bowmen demolished the 
127th Dragons.
  Dirkwood was overrun by the forces of Odysseus.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the 198th Trolls was greatly buoyed by the victory.  
We now rate it a proud Veteran unit.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I announced a call for 
volunteers in Dirkwood and was able to enlist the 91st Dragons to fight for 
me.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring, and I made ready to carry out my urgent orders. 
I spoke urgently to Everard and convinced him to pledge his services to 
Uga-Buga Makumb.  After talking to Everard, I judged him (a Elf well known 
for White Magic) to have an Evil, Berserk nature.
  In early summer, I rode into Jerbilia.  I encountered no monsters.
  With the coming of the late summer season Garin was resurrected by the 
