From: Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and I prepared to carry out my urgent 
orders.  I was instructed in the art of Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I 
studied and practiced my Necromancy and my skill in Necromancy went up.
  With the advent of the early summer season I was tutored in Necromancy by 
Uga-Buga Makumb.  I practiced for months and my skill in Necromancy 
increased.
  In late summer, I cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 282nd Skeletal Legion,
the 283rd Legion and the 284th Skeletal Chariots arose from the graves of 
the dead!
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to fall.  I marched on Katanga 
(#404) with my formidable forces.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, one can 
see a poor Mountain province known as Moongard (#405).  It is said that 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is the ruler there.  It is known to be 
populated by Orcs.  Their Orcish warriors fight as Axemen and Heavy Cavalry. 
To the west there lies a Mountain province known as Shasta (#304), a poor 
land of Eagles where Prometeo reigns.  If need be, they can call on an army 
of Eagles to defend their province.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Jungle province of Katanga, 
ruled by Circe (#8).  I commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders were 
led by Prometeo (#5).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Katanga (0404):

 283rd/VS  284th/AS  282nd/VS 
  Legion   Chariots   Legion  
    01        01        01    
------------------------------
    05     |||05|||  |||05||| 
 231st/V    24th/A   262nd/A  
  Legion   Hvy Cav   Hvy Cav  
                              
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my armies into the fray.  Prometeo commanded a host of loyal 
soldiers.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The two armies raced for the high ground, and I obtained 
an advantage by getting there before the enemy.  On the other hand in spite 
of my industrious planning, I was tactically outmaneuvered and soon realized 
that this affair would be an uphill battle.
  Prometeo started with an inspiring speech to his army, which bolstered 
their morale.
  Out on the left wing, the Veteran 283rd Legion were arrayed against the 
Veteran 231st Legion, who were stiffened by a hardened band of mercenaries 
of the Mercenaries Guild, who exhorted them to a fanatical charge by example 
of their experienced elan.  In this match, a rumor was circulated among the 
231st Legion that they would be given medals if they won the battle, which 
bestowed upon the 231st Legion the psychological advantage.  The 283rd 
Legion fought the 231st Legion and fought courageously, but was steadily 
pushed back.
  In the interior lines, the 284th Skeletal Chariots were arrayed against 
the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The squadrons of the 24th Heavy Cavalry experienced 
a tough challenge against the easily defensible Chariots.  In this area, the 
284th Skeletal Chariots were slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of 
ground and they joined the fight at a tiny disadvantage.  It seemed that the 
24th Heavy Cavalry might win the battle.
  Then the tide of battle turned.  A few of the soldiers of the 24th 
Heavy Cavalry got lost in a patch of fog, which whittled down their numbers 
slightly.  The 284th Skeletal Chariots battled with the 24th Heavy Cavalry 
and were bent back by their attack.
  On the right flank, the Veteran 282nd Skeletal Legion faced the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry.  The Heavy Cavalry troops bore down on the 282nd Skeletal 
Legion and shook them with the terrible impact.  In this sector, many men of 
the 262nd Heavy Cavalry were recovering from the flu, weakening their 
fighting spirit significantly.  The 282nd Skeletal Legion fought the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry and managed to make some slow progress.
  The host of Prometeo crushed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb's fighting spirit 
with one last push.  The 231st Legion destroyed the 283rd Legion.
  Pascal's armies were beaten and pushed out of Katanga.  I set out for the 
safety of Chaco with my motley army.
  In early winter, I attempted an illegal move.  I tried to move from Chaco 
to Cantia, a non-adjacent province.  Instead, I marched my command into 
Balmwood (#503).

  Thy humble servant,   Pascal


