IMPERIAL OFFICE REPORT

  Into thy heroic dreams cometh an apparition heaven-sent, to speak to thee of
thy progress in thy ambitions for Imperial Office.  It is not for mortal Kings
to know who rivals them for high offices, but the Divine One will allow you to
know thy place in the standings, and how thee compares to thy fiercest foreign
rival for each office (shown under "Riv%" as a percentage: your points divided
by your rival's points, times 100.)

Imperial Office           Best Hope     Rank  Riv%   Second Hope   Rank  Riv%
World Emperor             Uga-Buga Makumb  1   106   None
  An ethereal Emerald Crown appeared on Uga-Buga Makumb's head, and a 
booming voice heard only by Uga-Buga Makumb ordained "This is the Crown of 
the Emperors of the Ancient Dynasty which ruled this world thousands of 
years ago.  It is yours for as long as you are the best hope to become the 
next World Emperor, and can be given to no other.  The Crown will give you 
the ability to know the strength of all your rivals in your quest for 
Empire".  (This information will be shown in your Diplomacy report in future 
gameturns).  Only the tax bases of kings bordering your kingdom that you 
have known for at least one full turn will be shown.

Esteemed High Chancellor  Magnus           3    85   Amalric          5    78
Imperial Treasurer        Uga-Buga Makumb  2    92   None
Imperial Grand Marshal    Guerin           2   100   Uga-Buga Makumb   4    86
Imperial Grand Admiral    Tao-Li          18    19   Guerin          21    11
Lord High Defender        Clarambald       4     9   Gladstone        8     5
High Priest Palatine      Guerin           1   116   Teleko           2   105
Arch-Mage Palatine        Teleko           2    92   Gladstone        6    57
First Elder of Elvenkind  Guerin           1   933   Uga-Buga Makumb   2   266
Dragon Lord               Uga-Buga Makumb  2    54   Guerin           3    18
Ace of Eagles             Teleko           1  None   None
  The title of "Ace of Eagles" is given to the character who has best 
protected the race of Eagles and led them to martial glory.
  As the Ace of Eagles, Teleko has won the loyalty of the Eagle race.  Each 
Eagle wing directly led by Teleko has a 50% chance to become fanatical in 
battle, thus fighting at the next higher quality level.

Master of Elements        Clarambald       1   190   Odysseus         4    54
  The title of "Master of Elements" is given to the character who most 
distinguishes himself in the art of Elemental Magic.
  As the Master of Elements, Clarambald has attracted the loyalty of the 
Elemental Beings, which sometimes visit this plane.  They have sent an Air 
Elemental to Clarambald as a Wizard's Familiar.  Whenever she flees combat, 
the Air Elemental will form a whirlwind and whisk Clarambald away.  Thus, 
all flee attempts are automatically successful.

High Mucky-Muck of Trolls Teleko           1   100   None
  The title of "High Mucky-Muck of Trolls" is given to the character who has 
best protected the race of Trolls and led them to martial glory.
  As the High Mucky-Muck of Trolls, Teleko has won the loyalty of the 
Trollish race.  Each Troll army directly led by Teleko has a 50% chance to 
become fanatical in battle, thus fighting at the next higher quality level.

Angel of Death            Uga-Buga Makumb  1   106   None
  As the Angel of Death, Uga-Buga Makumb has become the most powerful Undead 
King in the world.  His infamy has attracted the service of Circle of 
Wraiths, a greatly feared band of wandering Undead wraiths who have banded 
together in the pursuit of greater power.  When Uga-Buga Makumb is the 
supreme commander at a battle, one non-skeletal unit in the front line, 
chosen at random, will be joined by a flight of screaming Wraiths and become 
fanatical.  Also, the Wraiths will help Uga-Buga Makumb in raising skeletal 
units: when he casts the Skeletal Armies spell, the maximum number of units 
that can be raised by Uga-Buga Makumb increases by 1.

Prince of Thieves         Presto           1  None   None
Royal Air Force           322nd Eagles     3    52   None
Praetorian Guard          108th Elf Bowmen  1   127   110th Elf Bowmen   3   103
  As the Praetorian Guard, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen has won recognition as 
the land unit most qualified to protect the future World Emperor.  Whenever 
they encamp with other armies, they spend their time telling stories of the 
great battles they have fought.  Their gallantry inspires their fellow 
soldiers to train more intensively, so that when the 108th Skeletal Bowmen 
trains other land units, their chance to improve in quality is doubled, and 
the chance for non-land units is increased by half.


  Note: Kings owning 6% of the world's tax base called for an election.   


